    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under load, fails predictably, and reports honestly. It is written for pre-production acceptance and post-change regression testing. Each item should be marked PASS / FAIL / N-A with evidence attached.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal: prove that every node is running the exact same logical system.**\n\n- [ ] **1.1 Model artifact hash.** Record SHA-256 of model weights, tokenizer files, and config files on every node. All hashes must match. For sharded weights, hash each shard and verify shard-to-rank mapping matches the launch plan.\n- [ ] **1.2 Code and container identity.** Record container image digests (not tags \u2014 tags are mutable), git commit SHA, and build timestamp for every process. Verify no node is running a stale image after a rolling update.\n- [ ] **1.3 Inference engine version parity.** Same version of the serving framework (e.g., vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, SGLang, DeepSpeed-MII) on all nodes, including CUDA/ROCm driver versions, NCCL/HCCL versions, and Python environment lockfile hash.\n- [ ] **1.4 Parallelism configuration.** Tensor-parallel size, pipeline-parallel size, expert-parallel size, data-parallel replicas, and their mapping to physical devices are identical across all launch points (launcher config, environment variables, per-node local configs). A mismatch here is a classic silent failure.\n- [ ] **1.5 Sampling and decoding parameters.** Verify the effective defaults (temperature, top-p, top-k, max context, KV-cache dtype, quantization config) as seen by the *server*, not just as written in",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
